<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the application bundle.

  A hardened runtime refuses these four things unless a bundle asks for them,
  and Electron is built on a JavaScript engine that needs three of them. Each
  entry is here because a component of the runtime cannot work without it, not
  because a build failed once and the entry was added until it passed:

    allow-jit
      V8 compiles JavaScript to machine code while the process runs. Without
      this the renderer falls back to an interpreter or dies at startup.

    allow-unsigned-executable-memory
      The same engine maps memory as executable after writing it. An older
      Electron needed this beside allow-jit; the pinned runtime is built for a
      macOS version that still requires it, so it is kept and named rather than
      removed and discovered.

    allow-dyld-environment-variables
      The runtime resolves a few libraries at load time.

    disable-library-validation
      The application ships its own libraries and loads nothing from a
      third party. The entry is kept because it is the one entitlement that has
      to be present for the runtime to load a library it did not sign itself,
      and a build that lacks it fails in a way that looks like a corrupted
      download rather than a signing mistake.

  Two entitlements are deliberately absent. There is no
  `com.apple.security.network.client`, because that is an App Store sandbox
  entitlement and this application is distributed outside the App Store: it
  talks to a loopback endpoint, which a hardened runtime does not restrict.
  There is no `com.apple.security.get-task-allow`, because that is the
  debugger attachment entitlement and granting it would remove the protection
  the hardened runtime exists to provide. A debug build asks for it with
  `--config.mac.entitlements`; a release never does.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
